              238683,
              90395,
              145901,
              279207,
              380695
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 238683,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing. From my experience with clinic operations, the patient flow in Option B could create a bottleneck near the reception. Option A's circulation path is much clearer. We could slightly adjust the waiting area in A to improve accessibility without a major redesign.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 380695,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "I prefer Option A. The structural grid is simpler, which should make it faster and cheaper to build. Option B would require a few transfer beams that could add complexity and cost.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 90395,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Have we thought about where the new HVAC units will go for these layouts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 145901,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "At this concept stage, MEP is schematic. Both layouts have allocated sufficient space in the ceiling plenum for ducting runs. We'll detail that out after a layout is chosen.",
